    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -210,
        "title": "WDM through an SOA \u2014 what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "Three CW lasers on a 0.4 nm grid (1309.6/1310.0/1310.4 nm)",
          "are each modulated by their own MZM + PRBS, combined onto",
          "one bus (bus_in shows the 3-line comb), and amplified by a",
          "SINGLE shared SOA. A demux (FLT1-3) drops each channel to",
          "PD1-3; amp_out shows the amplified comb sitting on the SOA's",
          "ASE floor, vout1-3 are the recovered eyes. Transient noise",
          "(seeds = 1) is on, so the ASE is a live noise source.",
          "",
          "At the default power the SOA is unsaturated (amp_out ~2 mW",
          "<< p_sat 10 mW) with high OSNR: the eyes are open. Push it",
          "off either edge of its power window and the eyes collapse:",
          "",
          "SATURATION -> set SOA1.p_sat = 1e-3 and re-run. The shared",
          "gain reservoir now follows the aggregate bit pattern, so",
          "each channel's gain swings with its NEIGHBOURS' data (cross-",
          "gain modulation) - the eye patterns shut (Q 10 -> 2).",
          "",
          "WEAK INPUT / BAD SNR -> set VOA.loss_dB_cm = 20 and re-run.",
          "The signal sinks toward the fixed ASE floor, OSNR collapses",
          "and the eye fills with noise (Q 10 -> 4; try 25 dB for more)."
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
